## 7. How Kohler makes money

| Source | How it works | Rough size |
|---|---|---|
| **Casino edge** | Games pay back 95.8–99% of what's bet over time; the rest stays | 1–4.2% of everything bet in the casino |
| **Survivor fee** | 10% of what losers put in *(adjustable)* | About 3% of everything staked (Classic), 2% (Squad), 2% (Blitz), 5% (Duel) |
| **Deposit fee** | 1% of each deposit *(adjustable)* | 1% of deposits |
| **Withdrawal fee** | 1% of each withdrawal; the Bitcoin network fee is passed on at cost | 1% of withdrawals |
| **Vault** | Avatars, Legendary characters, custom avatars, frames, effects, themes, Kohler Pass | Pure margin, minus a little AI painting allowance |

**A worked example.** One month with 500 active players, each depositing $100 and betting
their money around 10 times:

- Deposits: $50,000 → deposit fees **$500**.
- Total bets: about $500,000. With half in casino games at ~2.5% average edge, that's
  **~$6,250**. With half in Survivor at ~3%, that's **~$7,500**.
- Withdrawals: about $30,000 → withdrawal fees **$300**.
- Vault: 10% of players spend $10 → **$500**.
- Total: about **$15,000** before costs. Bonuses, marketing, licence, hosting and staff come out
  of this.

This is an illustration, not a forecast. Real results swing, especially in the casino.

**Costs to plan for:**

- **Bonuses:** invite bonus $5 to the friend and $10 to the referrer.
- **Licence and compliance:** see section 10.
- **Marketing and affiliates.**
- **Hosting:** Vercel and Neon, small at first.
- **AI painting:** Cloudflare's free daily allowance covers normal use; heavier models cost more.
- **Bitcoin network fees on sweeps.**
- **Support staff.**

## 8. Money you need in reserve (liquidity)

The casino pays winners from Kohler's own money. Over thousands of bets the edge wins, but any
single night a player can win big. If the hot wallet can't pay a withdrawal, trust is gone, so
you need a reserve.

**What the reserve has to cover:**

1. **Every player balance, all the time.** Players' money is a debt you owe. Keep at least
   100% of all real-money balances in BTC you control (deposit wallet plus hot wallet), never
   spent on running costs. Kohler Control shows total balances on the Overview.
2. **A big win.** Today, the largest possible single wins are high:

   | Game | Max bet × top multiplier | Biggest possible win |
   |---|---|---|
   | High-volatility slots | $50 × 2,000× | $100,000 |
   | Rocket | $1,000 × 1,000× | $1,000,000 |
   | Limbo | $1,000 × up to 1,000,000× | far beyond any reserve |
   | Mines | $1,000 × up to tens of thousands× | far beyond any reserve |

   **Before real traffic, add a maximum win per bet** (for example $5,000 to start) and lower
   the high-limit tables. Then size the reserve to pay several maximum wins in a row.
3. **A run on withdrawals.** After a big win or bad news, many players withdraw at once. Keep
   enough in the hot wallet for a normal day of withdrawals and top it up from cold storage.
4. **Bitcoin's price.** Balances are in dollars but the reserve is in BTC. A 20% BTC drop
   shrinks the reserve by 20% while what you owe stays the same. Keep extra, or hold part of
   the reserve in a stable asset.
5. **Bonus money.** It doesn't need cash today, but it turns into withdrawable money once
   wagered.

**A simple starting rule:**

> Reserve = all player balances + 5 × the maximum single win + 2 days of average withdrawals,
> plus 25% on top for BTC price moves.

**Example:** $20,000 of balances, a $5,000 max win and $3,000 a day of withdrawals gives
($20,000 + $25,000 + $6,000) × 1.25 ≈ **$64,000**.

**Wallet layout:**

| Wallet | What it holds | Where it lives |
|---|---|---|
| Cold | Most of the reserve | Hardware wallet, offline |
| Hot | A day or two of payouts | Derived from `DEPOSIT_MNEMONIC`, used by automatic payouts |
| Main (sweep) | Where deposits are swept | Set in Admin |

## 9. Running it day to day (operations)

**Every day (about 30 minutes once it's busy):**

- **Payouts:** clear withdrawals waiting for review. Each shows why it's waiting.
- **Deposits:** decide small or flagged deposits.
- **Alerts:** read the Overview alerts. The autopilot flags:
  - balances that don't match their ledger
  - withdrawals waiting over an hour
  - support tickets open over 48 hours
  - Survivor books out of balance
  - stuck rounds
- **Support:** reply to Help tickets. Players see replies in the casino and by email.
- **Hot wallet:** check it can cover today's withdrawals; top it up from cold storage.

**Every week:**

- Avatars and Legends: approve new portraits; price and limit new Rare pieces.
- Promos: check what bonuses cost against the deposits they brought.
- Revenue: Vault sales, Survivor and casino books.
- Test accounts: give out or take back influencer access.

**Every month:**

- Reconcile BTC held against total player balances.
- Back up the database (Neon has point-in-time restore; keep an extra export).
- Review admin access and turn on 2FA for every admin.
- Check that player limits and breaks are working.

**People and roles:**

| Role | Can do |
|---|---|
| Owner | Everything |
| Finance | Sees money pages, read only. No emails or contact details |
| Support (to hire) | Answers tickets. Today support uses the owner account; a support-only role would be a quick addition |

**Keys and backups:**

- `DEPOSIT_MNEMONIC`, the cold-wallet seed and `KEY_ENC` should be written down offline, in two
  safe places, known to at least two trusted people.
- Every admin uses two-step sign-in.

## 10. Legal and compliance

Not legal advice. Gambling law depends on where the company is based and where players live,
so work with a gaming lawyer before taking real money at scale.

**What you need:**

1. **A gambling licence.** Online casinos need one, and payment and ad partners will ask for it.
   The common options for crypto casinos in 2026:
   - **Curaçao** (Curaçao Gaming Authority, under the new LOK law): the most widely
     recognised of the two. Now requires a local company, local staff and an office, with real
     KYC and AML checks. Roughly €24,600 a year plus €2,050 a month in fees, plus setup and
     compliance costs. About 2–4 months to approve.
   - **Anjouan** (Comoros): the cheapest and fastest, about €17,000–30,000 the first year and
     a few weeks to a few months. Less recognised.

   Malta and the UK are far more expensive and strict. They're for later, if ever.
2. **A company** in the licensing country (the licence requires it), plus a bank or crypto
   payment partner that accepts gambling.
3. **Know your customer (KYC) and anti-money laundering (AML):**
   - checking identity once a player deposits or withdraws above set amounts (tiered checks are
     normal)
   - screening deposit wallets for stolen or sanctioned funds
   - watching for unusual patterns
   - keeping records

   Crypto doesn't remove these duties. Kohler doesn't do identity checks yet (see section 12).
4. **Blocking countries.** Block players from countries your licence doesn't cover or where
   online gambling is illegal. Usual examples: the US, UK, France, the Netherlands, Australia
   and sanctioned countries. Your lawyer gives the final list. Kohler doesn't block by country
   yet.
5. **Age 18+.** Stated in the rules today. Identity checks are what actually enforce it.
6. **Responsible gambling.** Kohler already has a daily Survivor limit, breaks of 24 hours,
   7 days or 30 days, and limits that only loosen after 24 hours. Licences usually also require:
   - deposit limits across everything
   - permanent self-exclusion
   - reality checks (a "you've played for an hour" reminder)
   - links to help organisations
7. **Fair games.** Survivor is provably fair. Casino games use a secure random generator with
   published RTPs. A licence usually asks for an outside test of the random number generator
   (an RNG certificate), or you can add provably-fair seeds to casino games as well.
8. **Terms and conditions, privacy policy, bonus terms, complaints process.** Written by your
   lawyer to match the licence.
9. **Tax.** Depends on the licensing country and where the owners live.
10. **Advertising rules.** Google and Meta only allow gambling ads from licensed, certified
    operators in allowed countries. Influencer content has to say it's an ad, and must not
    target under-18s.

## 11. Marketing

**What Kohler already has:**

- **Invite friends:** a friend who deposits $20 gets $5. The referrer gets $10 once the
  friend has bet $100. Everything is adjustable in Promos, including new campaigns.
- **Test accounts for creators:** influencers record real-looking play with pretend money.
  Label the content clearly, follow platform rules, and don't show it to minors.
- **Characters people remember:** the Legendary characters have names and lines, star in their
  own games, and some unlock only through Survivor. That makes them good social content (clips,
  memes, stickers).
- **Collector drops:** limited Rare avatars, one of ones and artist collaborations.
  "Only 3 exist" is a reason to come back.
- **Habits:** daily streaks, XP levels, badges, seasonal Vault items and the Kohler Pass.
- **Survivor:** short, social and easy to explain. Crew tables spread by link between friends.

**What to add:**

- An **affiliate program** that pays streamers and sites a share of revenue.
- **Telegram and X/Twitter channels** for drops, big wins and new characters.
- **Landing pages** per character or game, for ads where they're allowed.
- **Tracking** of which channel brings depositing players, not just sign-ups.

**Watch the costs:** a bonus is only worth it if the player it brings deposits more than it
costs. Check the cost of each promo against the deposits it brought every week.

